# Sandbox reference

Lookup tables for the containerised agent sandbox. For the commands, see the
[how-to guide](../how-to/run-the-sandbox.md); for the reasoning, see
[The agent sandbox](../explanation/sandbox.md).

## Directory layout

```
docker/
├── agent/          # Dockerfile for the agent container (Python + uv + just + agent CLIs)
├── searxng/        # SearXNG (self-hosted web search) settings
└── README.md       # quick start, links back to this site
```

## Recipes

| Recipe | Action |
| --- | --- |
| `just sandbox-build` | Build (or rebuild) the agent image |
| `just sandbox-init` | Generate missing secrets into `.env` (idempotent) |
| `just sandbox-enable-user-instructions` | Create a local, read-only override for selected global agent instructions |
| `just sandbox-up` | Start supporting services in the background |
| `just sandbox-shell` | Open an interactive shell in the agent container |
| `just sandbox-down` | Stop containers + networks (volumes stay) |
| `just sandbox-nuke` | Stop and remove volumes, including persisted agent logins (destructive) |

## Services

| Service | URL inside container | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| SearXNG | `$SEARXNG_URL` | Self-hosted, privacy-preserving meta-search proxy |
{%- if include_crawl4ai %}
| Crawl4AI | `$CRAWL4AI_URL` (default `http://crawl4ai:11235`) | JS-rendered fetches, Playwright + Chromium, markdown output |
{%- endif %}
{%- if sandbox_observability == 'langfuse' %}
| Langfuse | `http://localhost:${LANGFUSE_PORT:-3000}` | LLM-native tracing, cost + dashboards (v3, six containers) |
{%- elif sandbox_observability == 'mlflow' %}
| MLflow | `http://localhost:${MLFLOW_PORT:-5000}` (`$MLFLOW_TRACKING_URI`) | Classic ML experiment tracking (single container) |
{%- endif %}
{%- if not include_crawl4ai %}

No dedicated fetch service runs; agents use their native HTTP-only fetch tools
(static docs/APIs/RSS work, SPAs return empty shells). Regenerate with
`include_crawl4ai=true` to add a Crawl4AI sidecar.
{%- endif %}

## Generated secrets

Written by `just sandbox-init` (and during `copier copy --trust` when
`sandbox_auto_init` is on):

- `SEARXNG_SECRET` (always)
{%- if include_crawl4ai %}
- `CRAWL4AI_API_TOKEN`
{%- endif %}
{%- if sandbox_observability == 'langfuse' %}
- `LANGFUSE_ENCRYPTION_KEY`, `LANGFUSE_NEXTAUTH_SECRET`, `LANGFUSE_SALT`
- `LANGFUSE_DB_PASSWORD`, `LANGFUSE_CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD`, `LANGFUSE_REDIS_AUTH`,
  `LANGFUSE_MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD`

`LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY` / `LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY` are **not** generated — they are
created in the Langfuse UI after first login and copied into `.env` manually.
{%- endif %}

Missing required secrets make `docker compose up` fail loudly on the `:?` guards
in `docker-compose.yml`.

Prefer storing only 1Password reference URIs in `.env`, for example
`OPENAI_API_KEY=op://<vault>/<item>/OPENAI_API_KEY`, and resolve them with
`op run --env-file=.env -- just sandbox-up`. Plain Docker Compose treats an
`op://…` URI as an ordinary string and cannot resolve it.

## Persistent volumes

| Volume | Contents | Security note |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `agent-home` | Agent login caches and user-scoped state | Secret-bearing; removed by `sandbox-nuke` |
{%- if sandbox_observability == 'langfuse' %}
| Langfuse service volumes | Database, ClickHouse, Redis/MinIO data | May contain prompts, traces, and credentials |
{%- elif sandbox_observability == 'mlflow' %}
| `mlflow-data` | Experiments and artifacts | May contain sensitive model inputs/outputs |
{%- endif %}

## Optional host instruction mounts

`docker-compose.override.yml` is absent by default and git-ignored. The
`sandbox-enable-user-instructions` recipe creates it only after displaying the
detected standard Claude/Codex user-instruction paths and receiving confirmation.
All generated mounts are read-only. Existing override files are never
overwritten, and complete agent configuration directories are never mounted.
{%- if include_crawl4ai %}

## Crawl4AI

- **Auth:** `CRAWL4AI_API_TOKEN` required (generated by `sandbox-init`).
- **API:** standard Crawl4AI REST — `POST /crawl` with a JSON body; see the
  [Crawl4AI docs](https://docs.crawl4ai.com/).
- **Resource caps:** `CRAWL4AI_CPUS=1.5`, `CRAWL4AI_MEM=2g` (override via env).
- **First start:** the v0.8 image is ~1.4 GB — expect a slow initial pull.

Prefer your agent's native `WebFetch` for static pages; reach for Crawl4AI only
when JS rendering or clean markdown extraction matters.
{%- endif %}

## Networking

- **macOS / Windows:** `host.docker.internal` is wired up so the sandbox can
  reach a host Ollama daemon at `http://host.docker.internal:11434`.
- **Linux:** `host.docker.internal` is added via `extra_hosts: host-gateway`
  (Docker 20.10+). If it misbehaves, prefer `docker run --network host`.
- **Sandbox CIDR:** the network is pinned to `172.28.0.0/16` so you can target it
  in firewall rules.

## Resource limits

CPU and memory caps are set in `docker-compose.yml`. Defaults
(`SANDBOX_CPUS=2.8`, `SANDBOX_MEM=6g`) target ~70 % of a 4-P-core / 16 GB host to
avoid thermal throttling. Override via environment.
